    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263-a5">

                <pb facs="0456" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg384"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No.
                    332.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Mariscal to Mr. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-12-22"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 22,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have had the honor to receive
                    your excellency’s note of this date, in which, referring to the dispatch of the
                    Secretary of State of the United States, of the 29th of November, ultimo, you
                    were pleased to say to me that, by an error of copy, the date for the assembling
                    of the proposed peace congress should be the 22d.</p>
                <p>I renew to your excellency, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>IGNO. MARISCAL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
